{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":7039,"ns":0,"title":"Control theory","extract":"Control theory is a field of control engineering and applied mathematics that deals with the control of dynamical systems. The aim is to develop a model or algorithm governing the application of system inputs to drive the system to a desired state, while minimizing any delay, overshoot, or steady-state error and ensuring a level of control stability; often with the aim to achieve a degree of optimality.","description":"Branch of engineering and mathematics","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}